{
  "id": 234329037,
  "iid": 11322,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "DHCPFO: Add Microsoft-specific hostname options",
  "description": "This is related to issue #19178.\n\nSample capture with Windows Server 2012 R2: [dhcpserver-w2012r2-server1-failover.pcapng](/uploads/50492c3e6862fe98114ec370d191fabc/dhcpserver-w2012r2-server1-failover.pcapng)\n\n- 31 = \"microsoft-client-hostname\"\n- 35 = \"microsoft-server-hostname\"\n\nHowever, the hostnames are in some 16-bit character format:\n\n```\n0000   64 00 68 00 63 00 70 00 74 00 65 00 73 00 74 00   d.h.c.p.t.e.s.t.\n0010   63 00 6c 00 69 00 65 00 6e 00 74 00 00 00         c.l.i.e.n.t...\n```\n(for \"dhcptestclient\")\n\nApparently this does not work:\n\n```\n\tconst guint8 *ms_client_hostname_str;\n...\n\t\tcase DHCP_FO_PD_MS_CLIENT_HOSTNAME:\n\t\t\tproto_tree_add_item_ret_string(option_tree,\n\t\t\t    hf_dhcpfo_ms_client_hostname, tvb, offset,\n\t\t\t    option_length, ENC_UTF_16, pinfo->pool, &ms_client_hostname_str);\n\t\t\tproto_item_append_text(oi,\", \\\"%s\\\"\",\n\t\t\t    format_text(pinfo->pool, ms_client_hostname_str, option_length));\n\t\t\tbreak;\n...\n\t\t{&hf_dhcpfo_ms_client_hostname,\n\t\t\t{\"Client hostname (Microsoft-specific)\", \"dhcpfo.msclienthostname\",\n\t\t\tFT_STRING, BASE_NONE, NULL, 0,\n\t\t\tNULL, HFILL }\n\t\t},\n```\n\nI basically copied the logic from `vendor-class` option handling and used `ENC_UTF_16` instead of `ENC_ASCII`, but apparently that is not correct way because the resulting text is \"搀栀挀瀀琀攀猀琀挀氀椀攀渀琀\".\n\nAny suggestions how to decode the string in this kind of case? I already tried to declare the string as `const guint16` but that errors out when compiling.",
